From: Remora <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 7 Aug 2026 10:55:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] vtest: allocate R8 blobs via GBM, and admit 64K-aligned YCbCr imports

bd remora-e5x.35, the residual of e5x.34's route-around. Two independent
defect legs, separated by standalone measurement (tools/gbmchain.c, with
tools/nv12chain.c mode 5 as the control):

1. The ALLOCATION BACKEND. NVIDIA cannot correctly re-import a dma_buf
   backed by its own Vulkan host-visible sysmem export (kernel
   intermapRegisterDmaMapping failures; single-plane re-imports walk pages
   in REVERSE). The same bytes allocated through GBM on nvidia-drm --
   the allocator every Wayland compositor exercises daily -- re-import
   byte-perfectly. The GBM dmabuf still mmap()s (the guest is a container
   and maps the fd directly), gbm_bo_map works, stride comes out
   256-aligned, and the fd is the allocation's sole owner once the bo is
   destroyed.

2. PLANE-OFFSET ALIGNMENT. The driver maps dedicated YCbCr imports at
   64 KiB granularity (import reqs.alignment=65536; the kernel names the
   failure 'MMU: given non-contig 4KB pages for 64kB mapping'). An NV12
   import whose chroma plane starts at the guest's tight offset (480000)
   reads plane 1 as ALL ZEROS even on a GBM allocation -- the green
   preview exactly -- while the same buffer with chroma at 524288 reads
   both planes perfectly. NVIDIA's own native GBM NV12 layout puts chroma
   at 655360: 64 KiB-aligned, confirming the rule. The control shows
   alignment alone does NOT rescue a sysmem export, so both legs are
   necessary.

The GBM route covers ONLY the R8 spoofed blobs (the gralloc CPU-format
class: camera NV12, sw-decode YUV, c2 bitstream blocks), whose consumers
are the guest CPU and NVIDIA itself. Real-fourcc linear buffers -- the
decoder's RGBX output pool, the encoder's direct-RGB input -- keep the
Vulkan sysmem export: they are imported by the INTEL iGPU's VA driver,
and iHD refuses DRM_PRIME_2 import of an nvidia-GBM dmabuf outright
('vaCreateSurfaces failed: resource allocation failed', measured live as
a dead hw codec session on the first frame), while it imports the Vulkan
sysmem export fine, and SF's single-plane sampling of that class is the
one sysmem re-import that behaves. The e5x.34 128 KiB fd-size padding
carries over to the GBM path; libgbm is dlopened (VTEST_ALLOC_GBM=0 /
VTEST_ALLOC_GBM_NODE=... overrides) and any failure falls back -- loudly,
once -- to the old path.

The e5x.34 refusal policy migrates accordingly: vkr_image now records
whether a YCbCr create's explicit plane offsets are all 64 KiB-aligned,
and the import site admits ALIGNED dedicated YCbCr imports for every
context -- with the guest gralloc aligning its YUV plane offsets
(external-minigbm-gbm-mesa patch 0007), those read correctly, so apps get
the fast GPU path with correct color. Tight or implicit layouts keep the
refusal and their color-correct CPU fallback; SurfaceFlinger keeps its
never-refuse exemption (a refusal there is a dead compositor, measured).

